    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Order each set of fractions from largest to smallest.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{3}{2},\\ \\frac{2}{3},\\ \\frac{10}{12},\\ \\frac{8}{6},\\ \\frac{5}{4},\\ \\frac{2}{4}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3}{2}>\\frac{8}{6}>\\frac{5}{4}>\\frac{10}{12}>\\frac{2}{3}>\\frac{2}{4}$",
          "worked": "Use a common denominator of 12.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{2}&=\\frac{18}{12}\\\\\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{8}{12}\\\\\\frac{10}{12}&=\\frac{10}{12}\\\\\\frac{8}{6}&=\\frac{16}{12}\\\\\\frac{5}{4}&=\\frac{15}{12}\\\\\\frac{2}{4}&=\\frac{6}{12}\\end{align*}$$\nComparing numerators gives\n$$\\frac{3}{2}>\\frac{8}{6}>\\frac{5}{4}>\\frac{10}{12}>\\frac{2}{3}>\\frac{2}{4}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$2\\frac{3}{7},\\ 3\\frac{1}{8},\\ 2\\frac{2}{9},\\ 2\\frac{5}{9},\\ 3\\frac{1}{9},\\ 2\\frac{6}{7}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\frac{1}{8}>3\\frac{1}{9}>2\\frac{6}{7}>2\\frac{5}{9}>2\\frac{3}{7}>2\\frac{2}{9}$",
          "worked": "Compare the whole-number parts first. For the two numbers with whole-number part 3:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{8}&=\\frac{9}{72}\\\\\\frac{1}{9}&=\\frac{8}{72}\\end{align*}$$\nFor the four numbers with whole-number part 2:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{7}&=\\frac{27}{63}\\\\\\frac{2}{9}&=\\frac{14}{63}\\\\\\frac{5}{9}&=\\frac{35}{63}\\\\\\frac{6}{7}&=\\frac{54}{63}\\end{align*}$$\nComparing numerators within each group gives\n$$3\\frac{1}{8}>3\\frac{1}{9}>2\\frac{6}{7}>2\\frac{5}{9}>2\\frac{3}{7}>2\\frac{2}{9}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      }
    ]
